000700**************************************************************
000800*                                                            *
000900*   T R E Q U P D T                                  MA2-1   *
001000*    THIS PROGRAM ALLOWS MATERIALS CONTROL TO PROCESS        *
001100*    REQUISITIONS.  5 OPTIONS ARE AVAILABLE WHEN DEALING     *
001200*    WITH REQUISITIONS.                                      *
001300*     1) RELEASE REQUISITIONS TO PURCHASING                  *
001400*     2) IF THE CODE IS ON A REQUIREMENT ORDER THE CODE      *
001500*        CAN BE PLACED ON A SHIPPING RELEASE WHICH IN TURN   *
001600*        CLOSES OUT THE REQUISITION                          *
001700*     3) PLACE THE REQUISITION ON HOLD                       *
001800*     4) CANCEL THE REQUISITION                              *
001900*D    5) RESERVE THE MATERIAL (IF ITS AN ENG. REQ.)
002000*                                                            *
002100*   SUBROUTINES CALLED:                                      *
002200*                       1) TCHKBLKT.SOURCE                   *
002300*                       2) TGETBLKT.SOURCE   MA2-6           *
002400*                       3) TBLKTINQ.SOURCE   MA2-6           *
002500*                          THIS SUB. IS USED IN PLACE OF     *
002600*                          TGETBLKT FOR AKRON PLANTS         *
002700*                       3) SRELEASE.SOURCE   MA2-7           *
002800*                       4) SREQPRNT.SOURCE                   *
002900*                       5) TPOPRNT.SOURCE                    *
003000*                       6) CRESERVE.SOURCE                   *
003100*                       7) TALWONO.SOURCE                    *
003200*                       8) TREQINTF.SOURCE                   *
      *                       9) TGETBLK2.SOURCE                   *
      *                      10) CREQLOG.SOURCE                    *
      *                      11) SGETABPF.SOURCE                   *
      *                      12) SRSNCDPF.SOURCE                   *
003400**************************************************************
      *C
      *C  05/02/94  JEFF BUNGO  REQ #6488
      *C    GAVE SHIPPING RELEASES THEIR OWN PRINTER NUMBER INSTEAD
      *C    OF USING THE PO PRINTER.  IF THE SHIPPING RELEASE
      *C    PRINTER NUMBER IS NOT YET DEFINED THEN USE THE PO
      *C    PRINTER NUMBER AND UPDATE THE SHIPPING RELEASE PRINTER
      *C    WITH THE PO PRINTER NUMBER.
      *C
      *C   08/09/94  JE COFFMAN  WRITTEN REQUEST 94-001/SLS REQ 6487
      *C     ADDED THE ABILITY TO ALLOW 'SS' STATUS REQUISITIONS
      *C     THAT HAVE THE AUTHORIZATION FLAG SET VIA MP1 TO BE
      *C     PROCESSED. CODE WAS REMOVED FROM TREQ AND PLACED
      *C     HERE SO THAT MATERIALS CONTROL WOULD BE ABLE TO
      *C     MAINTAIN THEIR ABILITIES.
      *C
      *C   NOV. 1995 JE COFFMAN     SLS REQ#6591
      *C     ADDED CODE TO WRITE A RECORD TO THE MCORPREQ FILE WHEN
      *C     THE USER PLACES AN 'X' IN THE "TO CORP PURCH" FIELD ON
      *C     THE SCREEN. THIS WAS TO GIVE CONTROL TO MATERIAL CONTROL
      *C     REGARDING WHETHER THEY WANTED TO AUTOMATICALLY GET A
      *C     REQUISITION TO CORPORATE PURCHASING INSTEAD OF MANUALLY
      *C     RE-ENTERING THE SAME INFORMATION VIA IMS.
      *C
      *C   09/10/96  JEFF BUNGO
      *C     EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C     INCLUDE CENTURY ON REQ MAT CONT RELEASE DATE,
      *C     REQ DATE WANTED, AND RESERVE DATE PARAMETER
      *C     IN CALL TO CRESERVE.
      *C
      *C   08AUG1997   WL MCINTYRE
      *C     ADD LOGIC TO ALLOW USER TO SPECIFY A DEPARTMENT
      *C     NUMBER TO RESTRICT REQ SELECTION.  REQUEST ORIGINATED
      *C     FROM THE DES MOINES PLANT, WHO WILL NEED THIS FEATURE.
      *C
      *C   10/15/97    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     BASED ON PLANT SWITCH FROM PREQ, REQUIRE A USERID ON THE
      *C     REQUISITION TO NOTIFY WHEN MATERIAL IS RECEIVED AT THE
      *C     DOCK.  ALSO, VALIDATE USERID ENTERED AS A VALID USERID
      *C     ON THE SYSTEM.
      *C
      *C  10/27/1997        CA YODER
      *C    RE-COMPILED PROGRAM TO PICK UP NOTIFY USER-ID IN DSHIPREL.
      *C
      *C  11/7/97           JEFF BUNGO
      *C    ADDED LOGIC TO ALLOW DES MOINES (310) TO ENTER CORP REQS.
      *C
      *C  11/24/97          JEFF BUNGO
      *C    ADDED LOGIC TO STORE THE "TO CORP PURCH" FLAG ON MREQ.
      *C
      *C  11/25/97    JEFF BUNGO   REQ #97-017
      *C     ADD USAGE FIELDS FOR DIRECT DELIVERY.  DD USAGE
      *C     TO BE STORED IN ADDITIONAL FIELD AND TOTAL USAGE.
      *C     STORE ISSUE USAGE CALCULATED BY TOTAL USAGE - DD USAGE.
      *C
      *C  03/24/98    JIM COFFMAN
      *C     CHANGED TO VALIDATE THAT REQUISITIONS FOR CODED ITEMS
      *C     THAT ARE CONSIGNED CONTAIN THE VALID STOREROOM DEPARTMENT
      *C     WHEN THEY ARE RELEASED TO PURCHASING.
      *C
      *C  09/23/99    JIM COFFMAN
      *C     ADDED A CHANGE AT STEPHEN SEYMOUR'S REQUEST TO NOT ALLOW
      *C     THE APPROVAL PATH OF AN AUTHORIZED FLAGGED ITEM TO GO
      *C     DOWN THE STOREROOM DEPARTMENT'S DESIGNATED PATH IF THE
      *C     CODE HAS A DEFAULT DEPARTMENT ENTERED.
      *C
      *C  01/06/00    CA YODER
      *C     CHANGED REQUIREMENT ORDER REVIEW PROGRAM FROM "TBLKINQ2"
      *C     TO "TGETBLK2" FOR AKRON PLANTS.  THIS WAS DONE SO THAT A
      *C     REQUIREMENT ORDER COULD BE SELECTED FOR A RELEASE TO BE
      *C     GENERATED IN CORP. PURCHASING (SENT THROUGH MA4).
      *C
      *C  11/22/00    JE COFFMAN
      *C     ADDED LOGIC AT NAPANEE'S REQUEST TO OVERRIDE STOREROOM
      *C     REQUISITIONS THAT ARE FLAGGED AS REQUIRING AUTHORIZATION
      *C     APPROVALS TO ALTER THE EXPENSE CLASS SO THAT THE REQ COULD
      *C     FLOW THROUGH SHORTENED APPROVAL PATHS.
      *C
      *C  MAY 2001    JE COFFMAN
      *C     ADDED LOGIC AT JIM JEFFERS' REQUEST (LAWTON) TO USE THE
      *C     LAST WITHDRAWAL DEPARTMENT IF ONE EXISTED FOR THE
      *C     CORPORATE CODE INSTEAD OF THE DEFAULT DEPARTMENT FOR THE
      *C     SPECIAL EXPENSE CLASS HANDLING FOR APPROVAL PATH
      *C     SELECTION MENTIONED IN THE 11/22/00 NOTE ABOVE.
      *C
      *C  06/07/01    CA YODER
      *C     COMMENTED OUT LOGIC TO SKIP THE 64-UPDATE-QTY PARAGRAPH
      *C     BECAUSE THE UNIT PRICE WAS NOT BEING PLACED ON THE REQ.
      *C
      *C  11/29/01    CA YODER
      *C     NAPANEE HAVING A PROBLEM WITH SPECIAL LOGIC ADDED FOR
      *C     AUTHORIZATION FLAG.  FOUND THAT THE SAVE-STRMDEPT WAS
      *C     NEVER BEING INITIALIZED UNLESS CODE WAS CONSIGNED ITEM.
      *C     CORRECTED LOGIC TO ALWAYS FIND THE STOREROOM DEPARTMENT.
      *C
DCR01 *----------------------------------------------------------------
DCR01 *--- MODIFICATIONS FOR ARIBA BUYER
DCR01 *----------------------------------------------------------------
DCR01 *C  10/18/2002  DAN RAUCH
DCR01 *C     ADDED LOGIC FOR ARIBA BUYER BY APPLYING TO THE AS400
DCR01 *C     VERSION, THE FOLLOWNG CHANGES APPLIED TO THE HP3000
DCR01 *C     VERSION BY KAREN RAUTENBACH.
      *C                   -----------------------
DCR01 *C     IF ARIBA ENABLED (MPLTINFO ARIB) THE DETAIL ON PLTINFO
DCR01 *C     WILL SUPPLY THE LENGTH OF THE COMMODITY CODE USED FOR
DCR01 *C     PLANT AND CODES ENTERED WILL BE COMPARED TO MCODEFILTER
DCR01 *C     - IF FOUND - DO:
DCR01 *C          1)  SET ARIBA-ENABLED-YES TO TRUE
DCR01 *C          2)  WRITE REQUISITION TO LOG FILE
DCR01 *C          3)  SET HOLD-STATUS = "AR" - DON'T PRINT
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
DCR02 *C  12/02/2002  DAN RAUCH
DCR02 *C     ADDED LOGIC TO PREVENT REQ'S ALREADY PROCESSED FROM
DCR02 *C     BEING SELECTED AGAIN WHEN PROCESSING BY DATE.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
DCR03 *C  12/03/2002  DAN RAUCH
DCR03 *C     PREVENT SCREEN ENTRY OF HOLD STATUS = "AR" -- THIS
DCR03 *C     STATUS IS RESERVED FOR ARIBA BUYER
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
DCR04 *C  12/11/2002  DAN RAUCH
DCR04 *C     ALLOW ENTRY OF STATUS = 'AB' - BYPASS ARIBA PROCESSING
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
DCR05 *C  01/21/2003  DAN RAUCH   - DCR05
DCR05 *C     BYPASS  F4  PROCESS'G WHEN REQ BELONGS TO ARIBA BUYER
DCR05 *C     JUST DISPLAY "INVALID FUNCTION KEY" MESSAGE
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
VER23 *C  09/19/2003  BILL FONAGY - VER.  -TREQUPDTV23
      *C     ****** ARIBA BUYER - GLOBAL ROLL-OUT ******
      *C          ADDED LOGIC TO INCORPORATE CHANGES THAT ARE
      *C          NEEDED TO IMPLEMENT INVENTORY REPLENISHMENT
      *C          FUNCTIONALITY FOR THE GLOBAL ROLL-OUT
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
DCR06 *C  11/06/2003  DAN RAUCH   - DCR06   VER. - TREQUPDTV24
DCR06 *C     DON'T ALLOW A ZERO REQ QTY FOR ARIBA BUYER REQS
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
VER25 *C  11/14/2003  BILL FONAGY - VER. - TREQUPDTV25
      *C     ****** ARIBA BUYER ENHANCEMENTS ******
      *C      ADDED LOGIC TO INCORPORATE:
      *C        1. IF AUTH-FLAG IS MARKED 'X' WILL KEEP IN CSIS
      *C           ONLY AFTER EXCEPTION IS INDICATED;
      *C        2. IF FREE-VERBAGE IS MARKED 'X' WILL ALSO KEEP
      *C           IN CSIS AFTER EXCEPTION IS INDICATED;
      *C        3. WILL NOW ONLY LOG EXCEPTION WHEN 'AB' BYPASS IS
      *C           INDICATED UNTIL 'ENTER' IS PRESSED;
      *C        4. WILL NOW READ CATALOG FILE TO DETERMINE IF
      *C           REQ. IS SENT TO ARIBA, NOT COMMODITY FILTER
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
VER26 *C  12/10/2003  BILL FONAGY - VER. - TREQUPDTV26
      *C     ****** VDA WORKSHOP EHNANCEMENTS ******
      *C      ADDED LOGIC TO INCORPORATE:
      *C        1.  IF REPAIR-FLAG IS MARKED 'X' WILL KEEP IN CSIS
      *C            AND WILL AUTOMATICALLY LOG AN EXCEPTION
      *C        2.  IF 'ENTER' US PRESSED AND NO OTHER FIELDS ARE
      *C            'X'ed OUT, WILL CALL 'SGETAPBF' SUBROUTINE
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
DCR07 *C  03/23/2004  DAN RAUCH   - DCR07
DCR07 *C     RECOMPILED FOR SCREEN CHANGE (VERBAGE)
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
VER27 *C  03/24/2004  BILL FONAGY - VER - TREQUPDTV27
VER27 *C      ADDED LOGIC TO:
VER27 *C        CONVERT QUANTITY ON AN ARIBA ITEM FROM
VER27 *C        THE STOREROOM UOM TO THE CATALOG UOM IF
VER27 *C        THE UOM IS DIFFERENT.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
VER28 *C  06/22/2004  BILL FONAGY - VER - TREQUPDTV28
VER28 *C     MOVED "CANCEL" LOGIC TO BY PASS ALL ADDITIONAL EDIT
VER28 *C     CHECKS SINCE IT DID NOT MAKE SENSE, IF A REQUISITION
VER28 *C     IS BEING CANCELLED, TO GO THROUGH ALL THE EDIT CHECKS
VER28 *C     FIRST, THEN CANCEL THE REQUISITION.  NOW WE JUST
VER28 *C     CANCEL THE REQUISITIONS.  ALSO, REPORTED BY STEPHEN
VER28 *C     SEYMOUR IN NAPANEE.
      **************************************************************


